{
  "an6.63:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.63 ",
  "an6.63:0.2": "6. The Great Chapter ",
  "an6.63:0.3": "Penetrative ",
  "an6.63:1.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you a penetrative exposition of the teaching. ",
  "an6.63:1.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "an6.63:1.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "an6.63:1.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an6.63:2.1": "“Mendicants, what is the penetrative exposition of the teaching? ",
  "an6.63:2.2": "Sensual pleasures should be known. And their source, diversity, result, cessation, and the practice that leads to their cessation should be known. ",
  "an6.63:3.1": "Feelings should be known. And their source, diversity, result, cessation, and the practice that leads to their cessation should be known. ",
  "an6.63:4.1": "Perceptions should be known. And their source, diversity, result, cessation, and the practice that leads to their cessation should be known. ",
  "an6.63:5.1": "Defilements should be known. And their source, diversity, result, cessation, and the practice that leads to their cessation should be known. ",
  "an6.63:6.1": "Deeds should be known. And their source, diversity, result, cessation, and the practice that leads to their cessation should be known. ",
  "an6.63:7.1": "Suffering should be known. And its source, diversity, result, cessation, and the practice that leads to its cessation should be known. ",
  "an6.63:8.1": "‘Sensual pleasures should be known. And their source, diversity, result, cessation, and the pract